values
  (197, 'How slice 2.4 is built (`slice-2-4.md`). `GET /v1/sessions` lists the latest agent sessions from the database alone, never the runtime: each thread''s own session once it has one, and each change''s coding worker from its brief, even while it waits for Start. Each comes with its state, what it was asked, who asked, its project, the last thing it said (at most 200 characters), its list cost against its budget, and its thread. Working and waiting ones first, then by latest activity; ten by default, at most fifty. The service token and a signed-in person may read it, like `GET /v1/conversations` (194). The web app''s home page shows it to a signed-in person, server-rendered on each request, with a Refresh link and a link to each Slack thread', 'The Dashboard v1 plan''s page (SCRUM-7, SCRUM-11), with cost added: everyone may ask for anything (174), so what each session spends has to be seen (182). Reading the record keeps the page working when the runtime is slow or down, and adds no call while a sync lease is held', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-25T00:00:00Z', 'import', '197')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
